> Values only: explore a bounded multimodal function

For Rastrigin in two dimensions, f=20+x squared+y squared-10*cos(2*pi*x)
-10*cos(2*pi*y), the minimum is exactly zero at the origin. Local basins make it
a useful counterweight to the previous convex bowl. PSO moves a particle swarm
using personal and global best positions. Differential evolution mutates
population differences and retains improvements. The real-valued genetic
algorithm selects parents, crosses coordinates and adds Gaussian mutations.
All three native routines clamp coordinates to the supplied box and return the
best visited point. Their stagnation stops can end a run before its budget.

Use box [-5.12,5.12] squared, start (3,3), seed 42 and population forty.
PSO uses global attraction and its default constant inertia; DE uses rand1 mutation and binomial crossover
and default mutation/crossover; GA uses its default tournament selection,
blend crossover, Gaussian mutation and elitism. Each allows 500 iterations
or generations with tolerance 1e-12. Simulated annealing uses 30000 Gaussian
proposals, initial temperature ten, cooling .9995 and sigma .3 with the same
seed/start; its native API has no box. It is therefore shown separately.
Curves are labelled best *visited*, including accepted and rejected proposals;
they do not represent accepted-state paths. One seed cannot estimate success
probability, and neither an apparent plateau nor normal return proves global
optimality. Inspect the complete table, including any local-basin results.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/opt_overview_population.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace o = dm::optim;
  o::SmoothBenchmark        f("rastrigin");
  const std::vector<double> lo(2, -5.12), hi(2, 5.12);
  o::PSOOptions             p;
  p.max_iterations = 500;
  p.tolerance      = 1e-12;
  o::DEOptions d;
  d.population_size = 40;
  d.max_generations = 500;
  d.tolerance       = 1e-12;
  o::GAOptions g;
  g.population_size = 40;
  g.max_generations = 500;
  g.tolerance       = 1e-12;
  std::vector<o::OptimizationRun> runs{
      o::trace_optimize<o::ArbitraryFunction>(f, o::PSO(p), {3, 3}, lo, hi),
      o::trace_optimize<o::ArbitraryFunction>(f, o::DifferentialEvolution(d), {3, 3}, lo, hi),
      o::trace_optimize<o::ArbitraryFunction>(f, o::GeneticAlgorithm(g), {3, 3}, lo, hi)};
  const std::vector<std::string> names{"PSO box", "DE box", "GA box"};
  auto                           a = o::optimization_comparison(f, runs, names, "value", 0, true)
               .title("Bounded Rastrigin: best visited values");
  o::SimulatedAnnealingOptions s;
  s.max_iterations      = 30000;
  s.initial_temperature = 10;
  s.cooling_rate        = .9995;
  s.step_std_dev        = .3;
  const auto sa = o::trace_optimize<o::ArbitraryFunction>(f, o::SimulatedAnnealing(s), {3, 3});
  auto       b  = o::optimization_comparison(f, {sa}, {"annealing, no box"}, "value", 0, true)
               .title("Native annealing has no bounds");
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2).add(a).add(b).size(1100, 490).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/opt_overview_population.svg");
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < runs.size(); ++i)
    std::print("{}\n\n{}\n\n", names[i], runs[i].summary().to_md(8));
  std::print("Annealing\n\n{}\n", sa.summary().to_md(8));
}
```
